# =============================================================================
# RootLco — line-ending policy.
#
# Every text file is stored AND checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Why this exists: Prettier enforces LF (endOfLine: lf). On a Windows clone
# with core.autocrlf=true, a plain `git pull` checked the whole tree out with
# CRLF and `npm run format:check` failed on every file — see the Phase 1-2
# evidence register. eol=lf here makes checkouts deterministic regardless of
# any developer's local autocrlf setting; text=auto leaves true binaries alone.
# =============================================================================
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binaries (belt and braces; git's auto-detection also catches these).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
